==English==
{{wikipedia|in absentia (disambiguation)|in absentia}}

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|[[in]] [[absentia]]||in absence}}.

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP|head=in absentia}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} While not present; while [[absent]]
#: {{ux|en|The defendant was convicted '''''in absentia''''' after fleeing during the trial.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Workers World|author=Leslie Feinberg|url=https://ia804705.us.archive.org/23/items/lavender-and-red/Lavender_and_Red.pdf#page=77|title=Denazification in socialist Germany opened door to gay rights|date=28 Oct 04|text=The first chancellor of West Germany, [[w:Conrad Adenauer]] {{...}} continued to keep [[w:Hans Globke]] as his secretary of the chancellery despite protests. {{...}} Even after an East German court indicted Globke '''in absentia''' in 1950, Adenauer would not budge.}}
# {{lb|en|transferred sense|possibly|proscribed}} [[absent|Absent]] in general; not [[present]].
#: {{ux|en|Since then, the ex-minister has been '''in absentia''', likely relaxing on his private yacht.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Yuu Kamiya|translator=Daniel Komen|year=2016|title=No Game No Life|volume=4|text=At Sora’s involuntary acknowledgment of their crew currently '''in absentia''', Shiro nodded.}}

